<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dogras</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dogra</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dogras are a people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jammu">Jammu</a> region in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Dogra brothers, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulab-singh">Gulab Singh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhian-singh">Dhian Singh</a>, rose to great power at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>'s death in 1839 their factional manoeuvres contributed to the instability that led to the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> wars. Gulab Singh afterwards became ruler of Jammu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a>.</p></div>
